snow:
Night jasmines cannot bloom in this cold place;
Without the street is wet and weird with snow;
The cold nude trees are tossing to and fro;

snowy:
Alphenor saw, and trembling at the view,
Beat his torn breast, that chang'd its snowy hue.
He flies to raise them in a kind embrace;

snows:
I want him at the shrinking of the tide;
The old snows melt from every mountain-side,
And last year's leaves are smoke in every lane;

snowflakes:
Always I knew that it could not last
(Gathering clouds, and the snowflakes flying),
Now it is part of the golden past;

snowdraps:
Lookin' mighty white;
Snowdraps lak a feddah
Slippin' down at night.

snowman:
Evah t'ing is still;
Listen to de snowman
Slippin' down de hill.

snoozin:
Twell all de neighbohs hyeah me call;
An' you'll be snoozin' des ez deep
Ez if de day was made fu' sleep;

'Possum roam de wood;
Little baby snoozin'
Des ez ef he know.
